{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A formatted credential followed by enough output can leave a secret fragment in persisted output and model feedback."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failing check can expose a complete formatted multiline credential in persisted excerpts and feedback."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Overlapping registered credentials split across output chunks can expose the longer credential's sensitive suffix."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A redaction marker causes otherwise useful diagnostic text to be withheld in full."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Generic API and event payloads can be silently rewritten and given gate metadata they did not have."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An artifact containing terminal escape bytes can be served with different source text from the stored artifact."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A patch containing literal terminal escape bytes is altered in the review prompt, giving the reviewer inaccurate evidence."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"compat","trigger":"unusual","reason":"After rollback, an older release can misclassify a successful result as a blocking confinement failure when its normalized output contains the error phrase."}]}